Hi,

I have good news concerning the OpenPrinting Summit. We have a room for 
30-40 persons for all 3 days (April 8-10) now. So we will be able to do 
a Summit as we did in the last years in fall, but this time we can have 
joint meetings with other workgroups of the Linux Foundation and can 
also invite individual persons who attend the Linux Foundation Summit 
anyway.

I have also asked for 2 breakout rooms for two hours per day, but it 
will take a week until I get the answer whether we will get them.

So now we are at the point to work out a preliminary agenda.

Registrations are also possible already. You register for the Linux 
Foundation Collaboration Summit and mention "OpenPrinting Summit" under 
"Why would you like to attend the summit?" and/or "OpenPrinting" under 
"If yes, which workgroups?". The registration is here:

http://events.linuxfoundation.org/component/registrationpro/?func=details&did=2

There are no registration fees. Registrations get directly forwarded to me.

    Till
